WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.457
A for loop is a natural choice when you already have a collection of items to process.

00:00:05.457 --> 00:00:10.432
The customers list contains Ava, Ben, and Carla.

00:00:10.432 --> 00:00:19.155
Python takes the first value, stores it temporarily in customer, runs the indented block, then moves to the next value.

00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:28.012
Read the loop as “for each customer in customers.” That plain-language reading often makes loops easier to understand.

00:00:28.012 --> 00:00:34.881
This pattern scales well: the same block can process three records or three thousand records.
